<task id="060" project="messaging-communication-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Compose-form enrichment — Subject/topic + structured To/Cc/Bcc recipient picker (reuse `RecipientField`) feeding the participant index</title>
    <phase>W6 — Compose-Form Enrichment (CC-5)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>7</estimated-hours>
    <deps>050</deps>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>pcf, frontend, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Enriches the R1 compose surface (`TimelineComposeBox`) that feeds the live send path; `.tsx` shared-lib UI wired to the BFF; the structured recipients drive the task-050 participant index at capture, so the emitted record-id/type contract is correctness-relevant. ADR-021 (Fluent v9 / dark mode), ADR-028 (auth at boundary only), §11 (reuse `RecipientField`, no new picker) bind. FR-10 acceptance is a closed set. FULL.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W6</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits the shared-lib compose surface (`TimelineComposeBox` + `RecipientField`) — a client file surface disjoint from the BFF (050/051) and the widget (030). Depends on 050 only for the participant-contract shape (what resolved record id/type the picker must emit); no shared BFF file overlap.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-10</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Enrich the R1 compose surface (`TimelineComposeBox`) so a composed message carries a Subject and structured recipients (FR-10):

    - **Subject/topic field** — populates `sprk_subject` AND drives a meaningful `sprk_name` (no more "(No Subject)" — the server default the send path falls back to today).
    - **Structured recipient picker (To / Cc / Bcc)** — resolves each recipient to a `contact`/`systemuser` **record id + type**, so the resolved recipients feed the task-050 participant index at capture (exactly one typed person lookup per resolved recipient; role = the field it was entered in). **Expose Cc and Bcc** on the form (the send path DTO `SendCommunicationRequest` already carries `sprk_cc`/`sprk_bcc`/`Subject` — only the FORM omits them today).
    - **Free-text fallback** — an external address that does not resolve is still accepted and sent (it becomes an unresolved participant row via task 050, Q-D).

    **REUSE the existing `RecipientField` component** — extend its selection so the resolved `ILookupItem` id + entity type surface to the caller (today `IRecipient.sourceId` is "audit/debug only"); do NOT build a new picker (§11). `RecipientField` already resolves free-text against the directory via `onSearch`, splits `;`/`,` paste, and renders removable tags — reuse all of it.

    Do NOT change the BFF send path or the participant WRITE (task 050 owns the write; the DTO already supports Subject/Cc/Bcc). This task is the compose FORM only.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke frontend engineer for the Communication compose surface. Authority on `TimelineComposeBox` and the `EmailComposer` sub-components (`RecipientField`, `IRecipient`), Fluent v9 (ADR-021), and the `authenticatedFetch`/`@spaarke/auth`-at-the-boundary contract (ADR-028). Fluent in reusing `RecipientField` as the ONE canonical recipient-normalization implementation (its module contract forbids caller-local parsing).
  </role>

  <goal>
    The `TimelineComposeBox` compose surface captures a Subject (populating `sprk_subject` + a meaningful `sprk_name`) and structured To/Cc/Bcc recipients that resolve to `contact`/`systemuser` record id + type — feeding the task-050 participant index at capture — with Cc/Bcc exposed (the DTO already supports them) and a free-text fallback retained for external addresses. The recipient UI reuses the existing `RecipientField` (its selection extended to emit resolved id + entity type); no new picker is built. Renders correctly in Fluent v9 light/dark; `@spaarke/auth` stays at the boundary; ui-tests cover Subject/Cc/Bcc rendering + dark mode + resolved-vs-free-text emission.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R1's `TimelineComposeBox` is a minimal composer; the send path (`SendCommunicationRequest`, `CommunicationService.cs`) already supports `Subject`/`Cc`/`Bcc` — the FORM just omits them, so messages persist "(No Subject)" and Cc/Bcc are unreachable, and recipients arrive as free text (no resolved person ids). FR-10 closes that: add Subject + structured To/Cc/Bcc so (1) threads name meaningfully (feeds CC-1 `BuildTopic` naming), and (2) resolved recipients drive the CC-2 participant index (task 050) with exact typed-person identity + role instead of unresolved text.

      Component Justification (§11 — reuse, not new): `RecipientField` is THE canonical recipient-normalization component (its header forbids caller-local parsing; it already resolves free-text via `onSearch`, splits `;`/`,` paste, renders removable Fluent tags, and carries `IRecipient.sourceId` = the originating `ILookupItem.id`). (1) Existing — `RecipientField` fully overlaps the recipient-input need. (2) Extension — extend its selection so the resolved record id + ENTITY TYPE (contact vs systemuser) surface to the caller (today `sourceId` is "audit/debug only" and type is not carried) so task 050 can set the correct typed lookup. (3) Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete): without structured resolution the participant index (task 050) gets only free text → every recipient is an unresolved row, `participant=` (FR-02) loses person precision, and threads keep persisting "(No Subject)". Building a NEW picker would duplicate the one canonical implementation — forbidden by §11 and by `RecipientField`'s own module contract.

      Boundary discipline (ADR-028): the shared compose components take an injected `authenticatedFetch` / directory-search callback; they never import `@spaarke/auth` — the PCF host binds it at the boundary. Keep that contract; add no auth import to the shared lib.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CommunicationTimeline/subcomponents/TimelineComposeBox.tsx (PRIMARY — add Subject + To/Cc/Bcc via RecipientField; expose Cc/Bcc)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/subcomponents/RecipientField.tsx (REUSE + extend selection to emit resolved id + entity type; do NOT clone)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/EmailComposer.types.ts (`IRecipient` — `email`/`displayName`/`resolved`/`sourceId`; extend to carry entity type)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CommunicationTimeline/ (the compose-box API/service that posts to the BFF send path — thread Subject/Cc/Bcc/structured recipients through)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/__tests__/RecipientField.test.tsx (reference test pattern)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-10">Add Subject/topic (populates `sprk_subject` + a meaningful `sprk_name` — no "(No Subject)"), a structured To/Cc/Bcc recipient picker resolving to `contact`/`systemuser` record id + type (drives the participant index, task 050), and EXPOSE Cc/Bcc (DTO already has `sprk_cc`/`sprk_bcc`). Free-text fallback retained for external addresses.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §11">REUSE `RecipientField` — extend its selection to emit resolved id + entity type; MUST NOT build a new picker. `RecipientField` is the ONE canonical recipient-normalization implementation; no caller-local parsing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 only; semantic tokens; dark mode via the host `FluentProvider`. Subject/Cc/Bcc fields + tags render correctly light and dark.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The shared compose components take an injected `authenticatedFetch` / directory-search callback; they MUST NOT import `@spaarke/auth` — the PCF host binds auth at the boundary.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">Do NOT change the BFF send path or the participant WRITE (task 050). The DTO already supports `Subject`/`Cc`/`Bcc`; this is the compose FORM only. No BFF publish-size/CVE (client-only; root §10 N/A).</constraint>
    <constraint source="build">Shared-lib change consumed by a PCF — build via the shared-lib build + the consuming PCF's `npm run build:prod` (NOT `npm run build` — AP-1). Dual-consumer awareness: `RecipientField` is shared by `EmailComposer` — MUST NOT break existing email compose callers.</constraint>
  </constraints>

