  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test>The compose surface renders a Subject field and To/Cc/Bcc rows; sending populates `sprk_subject` + a meaningful `sprk_name` (never "(No Subject)") and `sprk_cc`/`sprk_bcc` — no console errors.</ui-test>
    <ui-test>A recipient resolved via the directory emits a `contact`/`systemuser` record id + entity type (drives the task-050 participant index); an unresolved free-text address is still accepted and sent (free-text fallback).</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Dark mode (ADR-021): the Subject field, To/Cc/Bcc `RecipientField` rows, and recipient tags render correctly under the host `FluentProvider` dark theme (semantic tokens).</ui-test>
    <ui-test>The existing `EmailComposer` callers of `RecipientField` still render + behave (dual-consumer regression — the shared component was extended, not forked).</ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The compose form captures a Subject that populates `sprk_subject` + a meaningful `sprk_name` — no message persists "(No Subject)".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">To/Cc/Bcc are exposed; Cc/Bcc populate `sprk_cc`/`sprk_bcc` (already in the DTO); a structured recipient resolves to a `contact`/`systemuser` record id + entity type that feeds the task-050 participant index at capture.</criterion>
